-- ownership (v2; R-5.13.1 with R-5.5.6): `Inner.eq = sameLength` is a
-- comparison written as an alias in an imported module. Its push is
-- `comparison_changes_value` in `Inner`, where it is walked as `eq`; `same`
-- here calls `==` on `Inner.T` and is judged as any call of a writing
-- function is. `Inner.compare = Helpers.always` names a function of another
-- module, walked there as no comparison: it is left unchecked, never taken
-- for a read-only one, and `less` applies `always`' class.
import Inner exposing (T)


pub same : T, T → Bool
same x y = x == y


pub less : T, T → Bool
less x y = x < y
